1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,648
My apartment costs twenty years of my life every single month, yet I pay it with a smile.

2
00:00:06,948 --> 00:00:15,252
Landlord Arthur says rent is due at midnight sharp. He holds a brass hourglass filled with glowing white sand.

3
00:00:15,552 --> 00:00:23,592
I press my palm against the glass. The glowing sand drains upward, stealing my youth to balance the ledger.

4
00:00:23,892 --> 00:00:31,740
My reflection in the hall mirror shows silver strands in my hair. I am aging backward in reverse.

5
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:40,224
Arthur pockets the full hourglass, tipping his hat as his own deep facial wrinkles miraculously smooth away.

6
00:00:40,524 --> 00:00:47,820
I used to think this city was expensive. Then I realized time is the only currency they actually want.

7
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:56,376
Tonight, the hourglass is empty before midnight. Arthur bangs on my door, demanding the balance I do not have.

8
00:00:56,676 --> 00:01:02,244
I open the door to run, but Arthur grabs my wrist. He doesn't want my years anymore.

9
00:01:02,544 --> 00:01:08,616
He whispers that this building isn't a rental. It's a farm, and my lease was up an hour ago.

10
00:01:08,916 --> 00:01:15,780
My apartment costs twenty years of my life every single month. Who is rattling your front door right now?
